<ArticleLayout title={page.title} hreflang={hreflang} description={page.description} canonical={page.canonical} author={page.author} date={page.date} ogImage="" bodyHtml={`<div class="entry-content single-content"><p class="wp-block-paragraph">The price of <a href="/product/choline-chloride-60/" title="Choline Chloride 60% Feed Additive – Corn Cob Carrier China Manufacturer Supply">choline chloride</a> in China fluctuates based on raw material costs, production capacity, and global demand. As a leading China-based export distributor, <strong>Dinweys Biotech</strong> provides competitive pricing and market intelligence for <a href="/product/" title="Feed additives">feed</a>-grade choline chloride 60% and 50% formulations.</p><h2 class="wp-block-heading">Current Choline Chloride Price per Ton (2025)</h2><p class="wp-block-paragraph">Below is a reference price range for feed-grade choline chloride sourced from Chinese manufacturers. Prices are indicative and subject to change based on volume, shipping terms, and contract duration.</p><figure class="wp-block-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Product</th><th>Specification</th><th>Price Range (USD/Ton)</th><th>MOQ</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Choline Chloride 60% Corn Cob</td><td>60% purity, corn cob carrier</td><td>$850 – $1,100</td><td>20 MT</td></tr><tr><td>Choline Chloride 60% Silica</td><td>60% purity, silica carrier</td><td>$900 – $1,150</td><td>20 MT</td></tr><tr><td>Choline Chloride 50% Corn Cob</td><td>50% purity, corn cob carrier</td><td>$720 – $950</td><td>20 MT</td></tr><tr><td>Choline Chloride 75% Liquid</td><td>75% liquid solution</td><td>$650 – $850</td><td>25 MT</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><h2 class="wp-block-heading">Key Factors Influencing Choline Chloride Pricing</h2><h3 class="wp-block-heading">1. Raw Material Costs</h3><p class="wp-block-paragraph">Choline chloride production depends on hydrochloric acid, trimethylamine, and ethylene oxide. Fluctuations in these commodity chemicals directly impact final pricing.</p><h3 class="wp-block-heading">2. Production Capacity</h3><p class="wp-block-paragraph">Chinese choline chloride factories typically operate at 70-85% capacity. Environmental inspections and energy regulations periodically reduce output, creating supply tightness.</p><h3 class="wp-block-heading">3. Logistics and Shipping</h3><p class="wp-block-paragraph">Sea freight from Chinese ports adds $50-150 per ton. Dinweys Biotech leverages consolidated shipping to reduce per-unit logistics costs.</p><h2 class="wp-block-heading">Supply Chain Advantages with Dinweys Biotech</h2><ul class="wp-block-list"><li>Direct relationships with ISO-certified Chinese manufacturers</li><li>Volume-based pricing through consolidated purchasing</li><li>Flexible payment terms (LC, TT, DP) for qualified buyers</li><li>Full quality documentation including COA, HPLC, and LC-MS</li></ul><p class="wp-block-paragraph">For current pricing and bulk quotations, <a href="/contact/">contact the Dinweys Biotech team</a>.</p></div>`} />
